0,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"December 18, 2025 - A dance rattle from East Sepik Province in Papua New Guinea. Rattles like these may form part of traditional dress, tied to the ankles of people dancing in traditional ‘singsings’ · Wooden pipes made of thin bamboo are used for music making and ceremonies.",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
1,Alor–Pantar languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alor–Pantar_languages,"May 23, 2026 - A more distant relationship with the Trans–New Guinea languages of the Bomberai peninsula of Western New Guinea has been proposed based on pronominal evidence, but though often cited has never been firmly established. The family is conventionally divided into two branches, centered on the islands of Alor and Pantar. Alor branch: Wosika, Abui, Adang–Kabola, Kafoa (Jafoo), Kui, Klon, Wersing, Sawila, Kula · Pantar branch: Blagar, Teiwa, Tereweng...",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
2,Category:Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Central West New Guinea languages (2 C, 3 P) Chimbu–Wahgi languages (1 C, 16 P) Cook River–Kolopom languages (2 C, 2 P) Duna–Pogaya languages (3 P) Engan languages (5 C, 10 P) Linguists of Trans–New Guinea languages (1 C, 1 P) Madang–Upper Yuat languages (2 C, 2 P) Morobe–Eastern ...",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
3,Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"June 5, 2026 - Trans–New Guinea (TNG) is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
4,TWG - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TWG,"March 1, 2025 - Trans-World Group, association of commodities traders controlling stakes in most of Russia's aluminum smelters · TWG Global, American multinational conglomerate holding company ... Search for ""twg"" on Wikipedia.",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
5,Proto-Trans–New Guinea language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Trans–New_Guinea_language,"January 1, 2026 - Proto-Trans–New Guinea is reconstructed with a typical simple Papuan inventory: five vowels /i e a o u/; three phonations of stops at three places /p t k/, /ᵐb ⁿd ᵑɡ/, /m n ŋ/; plus a palatal affricate /ᶮdʒ/, the fricative /s/, and the approximants /l j w/. Syllables are typically ...",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
6,Trans-New Guinea | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/1038/,"Tereweng twg, a language of Indonesia · Tanglapui 2 · Kula tpg, a language of Indonesia · Sawila swt, a language of Indonesia · Timor 4 · Bunak bfn, a language of East Timor · Fataluku ddg, a language of East Timor · Makalero mjb, a language of East Timor ·",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
7,A Trans superstar of South Pacific music- I'm Moshanty,https://www.losangelesblade.com/2020/12/15/a-trans-superstar-of-south-pacific-music-im-moshanty/,"August 27, 2021 - But for veteran LGBTQ filmmaker and longtime U.S. State Department Arts Envoy, Human Rights Ambassador, Cultural Affairs expert and film documentarian Tim Wolff, a chance encounter led to the incredible story of a transgender music superstar and Papua New Guinea national hero Moses Moshanty Tau.",Tereweng,Trans-New Guinea
